Living Room
The small living room contains a couch, coffee table, and two
armchairs. Pictures of various cousins adorn the walls along
with two of your aunt's wretched attempts at oil painting. You
can't help but notice that the carpet could use a good
vacuuming.

Doorways lead west to your father's office, north to your
bedroom, and east to the kitchen.
#
Bedroom
This is your domain and has been since your family moved here
when you were six. A nightstand with a Superman lamp sits next
to your twin bed. Posters of various anime characters cover one
wall. A pile of laundry, slowly but surely attaining sentience,
occupies the far corner.

The door to the attic is in the ceiling above the pile of
clothes. You can return south to the living room.
#
Kitchen
The kitchen contains a series of cabinets and drawers along the wall,
Alongside a island that sits in the middle of the room. Various utensils,
pots, and pans lie around.

The Living is on the other side of the westward door. The entrance to the garage
also lies to the south
#
Office
This work station has papers stacked high and the marks of many late hours spent working.
There is a desk sitting in the middle of the room with a computer on it. There is also a
 printer sitting in the corner on top of a shelf holding a large number of documents.

You can travel back to the livingroom to the east.
#
Attic
The dark and smelly attic has a number of bugs wriggling around. There is also a sereies
of pipes that connect to the AC, as well as a number of cardboard boxes containing
old and falling apart, Halloween and Christmas decorations

You can go down back to the bedroom
#
Garage
The Garage door is closed with an old Honda civic sitting in the room. Shelves line the walls
containing a series of junk items, as well as fishing rods, bikes, and gardening equipment. There
is also a pile of crushed cardboard boxes sitting in the middle of the room, that has been neglected
and not thrown away.

You can go north back to the Kitchen.
#
